 "notes": {
  "title": "internal_4 \u00b7 The block-shaped patch city",
  "meta": {
   "dates": "6 and 10 November 2026",
   "pilots": "ERKS, ALEX",
   "city": "BlockShapedPatchCityWorld"
  },
  "summary": "<p>Two pilots, ERKS on 6 November and ALEX on 10 November, in BlockShapedPatchCityWorld: 289 prism buildings that fill their blocks, on streets laid in turned patches so that no view runs straight across the city. ERKS flew two single-drone runs, three swarm runs and a third single-drone run; ALEX two single-drone runs, then two swarm runs. Each run's three goals were drawn afresh from the city's own buildings. Practice was flown in PracticeBlockWorld and not recorded, so every run here counts.</p>",
  "changes_title": "Changes since internal_3",
  "changes": [
   {
    "area": "City",
    "items": [
     "<b>BlockShapedPatchCityWorld replaces DiamondCityWorld:</b> windowed prism buildings, each filling its block to the back of a 3.5 m footpath, on streets laid in turned patches so that no long straight view crosses the city (<span class=\"code\">504f068a</span>).",
     "<b>Goals drawn from the city at every Play:</b> a goal is one building and the ring of buildings across the streets from it, with pedestrians walking round the ring; the goals, the hats and the target walkers change every session (<span class=\"code\">a662bc31</span>).",
     "<b>Landmarks on all four sides,</b> for orientation: a mountain range to the south, a lake to the north, wind turbines to the east, a TV mast to the west in line with the start road; made taller twice for this city's narrow streets (<span class=\"code\">56d24e45</span>, <span class=\"code\">980da54b</span>, <span class=\"code\">a58decfd</span>).",
     "<b>Denser street furniture:</b> border trees, benches and bins, bus stops, hydrants and payphones (<span class=\"code\">37ba79bf</span>)."
    ],
    "leads": [
     "BlockShapedPatchCityWorld replaces DiamondCityWorld",
     "Goals drawn from the city at every Play",
     "Landmarks on all four sides",
     "Denser street furniture"
    ]
   },
   {
    "area": "Swarm",
    "items": [
     "<b>A wider formation that flows round buildings:</b> S6's spread (d_ref 2.0) and shield (<span class=\"code\">f5d7d01d</span>); S7's slide round buildings and adaptive spread, which narrows the formation to 0.85 of d_ref in the streets (<span class=\"code\">7bf41e8c</span>, <span class=\"code\">e545e7f7</span>); S10's ellipse round each building's footprint in place of a circle (<span class=\"code\">37a6ccf0</span>).",
     "<b>The swarm starts as a hollow ring</b> of ten drones, none at the centre (<span class=\"code\">d736f6b9</span>)."
    ],
    "leads": [
     "A wider formation that flows round buildings",
     "The swarm starts as a hollow ring"
    ]
   },
   {
    "area": "Controls",
    "items": [
     "<b>The spread dial does nothing</b> while the adaptive spread is on, and <b>the gimbal starts level</b>, moving only once its dial is turned (<span class=\"code\">9b809bfc</span>).",
     "<b>The yaw stick turns the pilot at 40 \u00b0/s with expo in both conditions,</b> where it was 90 \u00b0/s with the swarm and 75 \u00b0/s with one drone (<span class=\"code\">7d1d0f28</span>)."
    ],
    "leads": [
     "The spread dial does nothing",
     "The yaw stick turns the pilot at 40 \u00b0/s with expo in both conditions"
    ]
   },
   {
    "area": "Display",
    "items": [
     "<b>No stitching:</b> the panorama is gone and every feed is 1920\u00d71080 (<span class=\"code\">d2bb65e0</span>, <span class=\"code\">83b3ad63</span>).",
     "<b>The screens are 1.3\u00d7 larger,</b> 60\u00b0 wide at 2 m (flown from ERKS's runs on; committed in <span class=\"code\">333b53bb</span>).",
     "<b>A dim room fixed to the real room</b> behind the screens, a grid floor and ceiling, against motion sickness (<span class=\"code\">c096133a</span>).",
     "<b>Steadier frames:</b> baked occlusion and walkers asleep far from every camera halve the main thread's time (<span class=\"code\">e33b8e92</span>)."
